  "description": "One ICacheProvider API over Microsoft MemoryCache or FusionCache, with typed and composite keys, expiry profiles, sync and async get-or-create with stampede protection, and one-line dependency injection setup.",
  "id": "Fayakun.Extensions.Caching",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-09T11:08:18.74Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "U4+eaiZO3YRw6QNNwBtThiX/m9TYcQgJSaedSB2PJ5IjUFKgVpWf5bb14InDZ+oAL90wEjH9SPADVXsunrpK7Q==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 72952,
  "published": "2026-11-09T11:03:32.943Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 (breaking)\n- Targets netstandard2.0 (.NET Framework 4.6.2+), netstandard2.1, net8.0 and net10.0.\n- Dependencies: FusionCache 2.9 and Microsoft.Extensions.* 10.0.\n- New: GetOrCreateAsync, SetAsync, Remove and RemoveAsync on ICacheProvider (breaking for custom implementations).\n- New: AddCache(type, options => ...) with KeyPrefix, UseFullTypeNames and CaseInsensitiveKeys.\n- AddCache now lives in the Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection namespace (remove \"using Fayakun.Extensions.Caching.Extensions;\").\n- MemoryCache provider: get-or-create now has stampede protection, so a factory runs once per key even under concurrency.\n- Keys: namespace-qualified type names by default (A.User and B.User no longer collide), culture-invariant formatting,\n  and string values no longer share the \"Char\" prefix. Cache key strings differ from v1.",
